{
  "id": "COMPOUND:20369 - PROTEIN:5832",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Tectoruside may interact with HuT78 through a series of molecular targets. Tectoruside is implicated in targeting VMRC-LCP, which is a target of multiple compounds, including Methylseleno carboxyethylglutamine, Ginsenoside R10, and 7-O-Methylmangiferin. These compounds all share a common pathway of acting on VMRC-LCP, which in turn targets HuT78. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, suggesting that Tectoruside may exert its effects through a similar mechanism, possibly by modulating VMRC-LCP and subsequently influencing HuT78. The overlapping targets and the consistent pathway from Tectoruside to HuT78 imply a plausible, mechanistically linked interaction. However, further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct involvement of Tectoruside in HuT78 regulation and to elucidate the precise molecular interactions involved.",
